-- Hand-written question-specific interview answers; preserves existing option effects.
-- Idempotent: question_text is unique in the live catalogue.
WITH tailored(question_text, a, b, c, d) AS (
VALUES
('Do you ever compete with each other for attention?', 'We make sure everyone gets their moment on stage.', 'A little competition keeps us sharp, but we share the spotlight.', 'Of course; nobody joins a band to hide at the back.', 'Only when someone steals my solo.'),
('Do you think every member gets enough credit?', 'Every member deserves recognition for what they contribute.', 'We talk openly about credits before a release.', 'Some people get headlines while others do the hard work.', 'Ask our drummer how much press they get.'),
('Has anyone ever seriously threatened to quit?', 'We''ve had hard conversations, but we work through them.', 'Everyone needs space when tensions run high.', 'There have been moments when the door nearly slammed.', 'I''m not handing you a list of names today.'),
('How are major band decisions actually made?', 'We listen to everyone and aim for a shared decision.', 'We debate the options, then commit as a team.', 'The strongest argument wins, not the loudest voice.', 'Usually after three arguments and terrible coffee.'),
('Is friendship more important than musicianship in a band?', 'Friendship is what gets us through the difficult days.', 'You need both trust and the ability to play.', 'I''d take a brilliant musician I respect over a fake friend.', 'Friendship doesn''t fix a missed downbeat.'),
('What happens when one member hates a new song?', 'We listen to their concerns and try another arrangement.', 'We rehearse it before making a final call.', 'One person doesn''t get to veto everyone else''s best idea.', 'They can skip that track at the next rehearsal.'),
('What keeps the band together when things get difficult?', 'Remembering the music we want to make together.', 'We talk honestly and give each other space.', 'We refuse to let one bad night define the band.', 'Stubbornness and the fact we share a van.'),
('Who in the band is most likely to start an argument?', 'Anyone who cares enough about a song can get heated.', 'It depends on the issue, not a single personality.', 'Usually the person who thinks their part was cut.', 'Nice try; I''m not naming names on air.'),
('Who is most obsessed with the band''s success?', 'We all want this to work, just in different ways.', 'Some chase charts while others obsess over the next show.', 'The one checking ticket sales before breakfast.', 'Probably whoever booked this interview.'),
('Who is the hardest member to live with on tour?', 'Touring tests everyone''s patience, including mine.', 'We rotate chores so nobody becomes the villain.', 'The person who treats the tour bus like their bedroom.', 'Whoever snores loudest wins that prize.'),
('Do you think outrage helps sell records?', 'Controversy can bring attention, but the music has to last.', 'It might boost a headline without building real fans.', 'Outrage sells clicks faster than it sells good albums.', 'Maybe I should annoy someone before every release.'),
('Have you ever been misquoted in a way that damaged your reputation?', 'Yes, and it taught me to choose my words carefully.', 'I''ve asked for corrections when quotes lost their context.', 'A dramatic headline can make a calm answer look explosive.', 'Print this exactly: context matters.'),
('Have you ever deliberately caused controversy for attention?', 'No; I''d rather people talk about our songs.', 'We''ve made provocative choices, but not as a publicity stunt.', 'Sometimes an uncomfortable truth deserves the spotlight.', 'If I had, I wouldn''t ruin the trick by admitting it.'),
('Have you ever said something publicly that you genuinely regretted?', 'Yes, and I apologised when I got it wrong.', 'I try to correct mistakes instead of pretending they didn''t happen.', 'I''ve learned that an unfiltered reaction has a price.', 'Can I have a lawyer before answering that?'),
('Is being provocative part of rock music''s job?', 'Rock can challenge people without cruelty.', 'Provocation works when there''s something meaningful behind it.', 'If rock never unsettles anyone, it''s getting too comfortable.', 'A little trouble beats another polite anthem.'),
('Is there anything you would refuse to apologise for?', 'I won''t apologise for making the music we believe in.', 'I can defend my principles and still own my mistakes.', 'I won''t apologise just because our sound annoys someone.', 'I''ll apologise for the noise when the neighbours do.'),
('Should artists be expected to comment on every major issue?', 'Artists should speak when they understand the issue.', 'Silence can be more responsible than an uninformed statement.', 'We should have the freedom to speak, not a duty to perform.', 'I barely know what day it is on tour.'),
('Should old comments be held against artists forever?', 'People deserve room to learn and change.', 'Past words matter, but so does what someone does next.', 'Accountability isn''t the same as permanent exile.', 'If every old comment counted forever, nobody could grow.'),
('Where do you draw the line between honesty and offending people?', 'I try to be truthful without punching down.', 'Intent matters, but I listen when someone says I hurt them.', 'Discomfort isn''t always proof you''ve done something wrong.', 'Apparently somewhere before my next publicist calls.'),
('Would you cancel a show because of public pressure?', 'I''d first consider the safety of fans and crew.', 'We''d weigh the circumstances instead of reacting to headlines.', 'A noisy campaign alone wouldn''t make me cancel.', 'Good luck keeping us offstage with a hashtag.'),
('Do arguments in the studio ever improve the music?', 'Yes; a good debate can reveal a stronger arrangement.', 'We test competing ideas by recording both versions.', 'Some of our best riffs came from stubborn disagreements.', 'The shouting stops when someone finally plays the right chord.'),
('Do you prefer writing alone or with the whole band?', 'I love bringing a rough idea to everyone to shape together.', 'It depends whether the song starts with lyrics or a jam.', 'Writing alone lets me take bigger creative risks.', 'Together, until everyone suggests a different chorus.'),
('Have you ever thrown away a song everyone else loved?', 'Yes, when it didn''t feel honest to me.', 'We''ve shelved promising songs and returned to them later.', 'Popularity in the rehearsal room doesn''t make a song good.', 'I probably deleted the demo by accident.'),
('How do you handle writer''s block?', 'I step away, listen to something new, then try again.', 'We switch instruments or write without judging the first draft.', 'I force out ten bad ideas until one catches fire.', 'I stare at the blank page until it apologises.'),
('How do you know when a song is actually finished?', 'When every section serves the feeling of the song.', 'When another revision would only change details.', 'When the chorus hits so hard nobody asks for more.', 'When the band threatens to confiscate my laptop.'),
('How much of your real life ends up in your lyrics?', 'A lot; even fictional stories begin with real feelings.', 'I blend personal experiences with invented characters.', 'The songs are more revealing than my interviews.', 'Enough that some people recognise themselves.'),
('What makes a lyric feel honest rather than forced?', 'The words have to sound like something I''d actually say.', 'I remove lines that explain too much or chase a rhyme.', 'An imperfect truth beats a beautifully empty slogan.', 'If it sounds like a greeting card, it''s gone.'),
('What part of songwriting do you find hardest?', 'Turning a strong idea into a complete second verse.', 'Knowing when to stop editing the arrangement.', 'Writing a chorus that deserves to be shouted back.', 'Agreeing on a title without starting a civil war.'),
('What usually comes first when you start writing a new song?', 'Usually a melody that I can''t stop humming.', 'Sometimes a lyric or drum groove sparks everything.', 'The riff arrives first and demands a song around it.', 'Usually the deadline.'),
('Would you ever rewrite a song because fans disliked it live?', 'I''d listen to what felt flat and try a better version.', 'We might adjust the tempo or arrangement on tour.', 'I''d rather challenge the crowd than chase applause.', 'If they hate it, maybe we''ll play it twice.'),
('Do critics understand what your band is trying to do?', 'Some really listen; others hear a different band in their heads.', 'A review is one person''s perspective, not a final verdict.', 'The best critics challenge us without telling us what to be.', 'They could ask us before explaining our own album.'),
('Do you think some publications decide their opinion before hearing the music?', 'A few may, but thoughtful criticism still exists.', 'We try to judge reviews by their arguments.', 'Some headlines are written before the first chord plays.', 'A bad review makes a convenient publicity poster.'),
('Does negative press motivate you or get under your skin?', 'It stings, then I put the energy into practicing.', 'I look for useful criticism and ignore personal attacks.', 'A brutal review can make the next show even louder.', 'I say I don''t care, then read it three times.'),
('Have reviewers ever been right about one of your weaknesses?', 'Yes; a tough review exposed a weak arrangement.', 'Feedback can hurt and still help us improve.', 'A critic once heard a flaw we''d refused to admit.', 'Don''t tell them I said they were right.'),
('Have you ever confronted a journalist over something they wrote?', 'I''ve asked for a conversation when a piece was unfair.', 'We prefer requesting a correction over starting a feud.', 'If someone invents a quote, I will challenge it publicly.', 'I drafted an angry response and wisely deleted it.'),
('How do you react when a new release gets poor reviews?', 'We listen, learn what we can, and keep making music.', 'I compare the criticism with how fans respond.', 'One bad score isn''t going to rewrite our sound.', 'I turn up the speakers until I can''t hear the reviews.'),
('How much should artists explain themselves after controversy?', 'Explain what happened and take responsibility when necessary.', 'A clear statement helps more than endless arguments.', 'Artists owe honesty, not a hundred defensive interviews.', 'One apology shouldn''t become a full promotional tour.'),
('Is music criticism still relevant?', 'Yes; thoughtful reviews help people discover new music.', 'Criticism matters when it offers more than a star rating.', 'The best writers push music forward, not just judge it.', 'Ask a critic to play the riff before scoring it.'),
('What''s the harshest review you''ve ever read about yourself?', 'One dismissed months of work in a single sentence.', 'The hardest reviews are the ones with a grain of truth.', 'Someone called our sound all volume and no ideas.', 'It was so cruel I nearly framed it.'),
('Would you rather be ignored or hated by critics?', 'I''d rather someone engage with our music honestly.', 'A strong reaction is better than no conversation at all.', 'Hate us loudly; at least people will find the record.', 'Ignore me and I''ll just book a louder venue.'),
('Do meet-and-greets feel genuine or like part of the job?', 'Meeting the people who listen is genuinely special.', 'They take planning, but the conversations are real.', 'Fans can tell immediately if an artist is faking it.', 'It''s only awkward when someone asks me to sing.'),
('Do you read what fans say about you online?', 'I read some messages, especially stories about the music.', 'We check feedback without living in the comments.', 'I''ll read praise and criticism on my own terms.', 'Yes, even when I know I absolutely shouldn''t.'),
('Do you remember the people who supported you before you were successful?', 'Absolutely; those early faces still mean a lot to us.', 'We try to thank the people who came to tiny shows.', 'Early supporters earned more loyalty than any chart position.', 'Some of them still remind us how bad our first gig was.'),
('Have fans ever changed your mind about a song?', 'Yes; hearing it sung back changed how I felt about it.', 'A live reaction made us rethink an arrangement.', 'Fans sometimes hear the hook we nearly cut.', 'They loved the song I wanted to bury.'),
('How do you feel when fans criticise a new direction?', 'I respect that change can be difficult for listeners.', 'We hear concerns without abandoning our creative instincts.', 'I won''t make the same record forever to keep everyone happy.', 'They can complain after they''ve heard the whole album.'),
('How much do you think you owe your fanbase?', 'We owe them effort, honesty, and a great live show.', 'Their support deserves respect, not access to everything.', 'Fans make our career possible, but can''t write our songs.', 'At least a working encore and a decent merch table.'),
('Should fans be allowed to film entire concerts?', 'A few clips are fine, but I want people present too.', 'I''d prefer reasonable filming rules over blanket bans.', 'A sea of phones can drain the energy from the room.', 'If you film the whole set, at least get my good side.'),
('What''s the best thing a fan has ever done for you?', 'A fan once told us a song helped them through a rough time.', 'Seeing someone travel miles for a small show was moving.', 'They turned our lyric into a handmade banner.', 'They brought snacks when the tour bus broke down.'),
('What''s the strangest fan request you''ve received?', 'Someone asked us to write a song about their pet.', 'We''ve had wonderfully unusual requests at the merch stand.', 'One person wanted a signature on their guitar case mid-show.', 'I''ll never understand why they wanted my shoelaces.'),
('Would you rather have a small obsessive fanbase or mass casual appeal?', 'A devoted community means more to me than fleeting attention.', 'I''d love wider reach without losing our core fans.', 'Give me the crowd that knows every deep cut.', 'Mass appeal sounds nice until you can''t buy groceries.')
)
UPDATE public.interview_questions AS q SET
 option_a_text=t.a, option_b_text=t.b, option_c_text=t.c, option_d_text=t.d
FROM tailored AS t WHERE q.question_text=t.question_text
AND q.created_at::date = DATE '2026-09-02';